.TH DSH 1 "2026-11-26" "deepseek-harness" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dsh \- DeepSeek Harness command-line launcher and Web UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dsh
[\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIname\fR] \fIname\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIapp-args\fR...]
.br
.B dsh web
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIaddress\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-open\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
DeepSeek Harness is an open-source agent harness built on an
everything-is-a-plugin architecture.  The
.B dsh
launcher boots a named profile: an ordered stack of plugin-bundle patch
layers under the user's own overrides.  The
.B web
profile serves the browser user interface, by default at
http://127.0.0.1:3080.
.PP
This package installs the Web UI as a systemd \fIuser\fR service named
\fBdsh-web\fR.  It runs as the logged-in user, never as root, and keeps its
state under \fI~/.dsh\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B web
Boot the Web UI profile.  Accepts
.BR \-\-host ,
.BR \-\-port ,
.BR \-\-no\-open ,
.BR \-\-public\-url ,
and TLS flags; see \fBdsh web \-\-help\fR.
.TP
.B headless
Answer one task, print the result, and exit.
.TP
.B plugin
Manage a profile's plugin dependencies by forwarding to pnpm:
\fBdsh plugin \-\-profile\fR \fIname\fR \fIpnpm-args\fR.
The package bundles a pinned pnpm, so no separate install is needed.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.SH SERVICE
.TP
.B systemctl \-\-user status dsh-web
Show the user service state.
.TP
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now dsh-web
Enable and start the Web UI for the current user.
.TP
.B journalctl \-\-user \-u dsh-web \-f
Follow the service log.
.TP
.B dsh-web-url
Print the tokenized URL that opens the current Web UI session.
.PP
The first visit must use the tokenized URL printed to the user journal and
returned by \fBdsh\-web\-url\fR; a successful visit mints a persistent browser
cookie, after which the clean loopback URL works.  The optional file
\fI~/.config/dsh/web.env\fR supplies environment variables
such as \fBDEEPSEEK_API_KEY\fR and \fBDSH_HOME\fR to the service.  Use
\fBsystemctl \-\-user edit dsh-web\fR to change the bind address or port.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dsh
User sessions, profiles, credentials, and settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dsh/web.env
Optional service environment.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/dsh-web.service
The user unit (never a system unit).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSH_HOME
Override the harness home directory (default \fI~/.dsh\fR).
.TP
.B DSH_NODE
Node.js executable used by the \fB/usr/bin/dsh\fR launcher.
.TP
.B DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
API key read by the model provider configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
Upstream documentation: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
